<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech 1.IF Zivno sees higher 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Czech 1.IF Zivno sees higher 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary results showed calendar year 1996 net profit of Czech investment fund 1st IF Zivnobanka rose to 83.149 million crowns from 71.329 million for the previous year, its manager ZB Trust said on Thursday.</p>
<p>(in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> net result	    83.149 profit  vs    71.329 profit</p>
<p> operating result    58.261 loss    vs    45.572 loss</p>
<p> financial yield  3,331.794	   vs 1,058.314</p>
<p> financial costs     14.330	   vs   935.032</p>
<p> total assets     2,854.531	   vs 2,398.881</p>
<p> basic capital    1,962.103	   vs 1,962.204</p>
<p>Note. The fund's manager has yet to announce dividend plans for 1996 earnings. It paid a gross dividend of 15 crowns per share on 1995 earnings.</p>
<p>-- Prague newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
